00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Evil Dead Rise is a 2023 American supernatural horror
film written and directed by Lee Cronin.

11
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
The film stars Lily Sullivan and Alyssa Sutherland as two estranged
sisters trying to survive and save their family from Deadites.

12
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Morgan Davies, Gabrielle Echols, and Nell Fisher (in her
film debut) appear in supporting roles.

13
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
The film's development was preceded by scrapped plans for direct sequels to Evil Dead (2013) and
Army of Darkness (1992), and a fourth season of Ash vs Evil Dead (2015–2018).

14
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
By October 2019, Sam Raimi announced that a new film was in development, with Rob Tapert producing,
Raimi and Bruce Campbell executive producing, and Cronin writing and directing the project.

15
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
New Line Cinema (the first film's distributor) was
announced as a production company involved.

16
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:06,000
Principal photography took place in New Zealand from June to October 2021.

17
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
The film was originally set to premiere on the streaming
service HBO Max, but distributor Warner Bros.

18
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
Pictures opted to release the film theatrically
first after positive test screenings.

19
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
Evil Dead Rise had its world premiere at South by Southwest on March 15, 2023, and was
theatrically released in the United States on April 21, 2023, by Warner Bros.

20
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
The film received positive reviews from critics and grossed $147 million
worldwide, becoming the highest-grossing film of the series.

21
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
At the 51st Saturn Awards, it earned two nominations:
Best Horror Film and Best Make-up.

22
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:06,000
The film explores themes of sibling relationship,
pregnancy, earthquake, gore, sequel.

23
01:32:00,000 --> 01:32:06,000
The tone is dark and intense.
